Lost & Found Campus App is a Flutter-based mobile application designed to help students and staff efficiently report, search, and recover lost items within a college campus. 
The application provides separate options for reporting lost items and found items, along with details such as item name, category, description, date, location, and image. 
Users can browse and search reported items, view item details, and contact the person who posted the item.
The main objective of the application is to provide a simple, centralized, and user-friendly platform for managing lost and found belongings on campus. 
The system can maintain the status of items as Lost, Found, or Returned, making it easier to track the recovery process.
The application is developed using Flutter and Dart, with local storage or Firebase as the backend. 
This project demonstrates practical implementation of mobile application concepts such as user interfaces, navigation, forms, data storage, image handling, and search functionality.
